<title>UK: Baltic, Black Sea oil exports fall 0.3 mbpd on wee.</title>
<headline>Baltic, Black Sea oil exports fall 0.3 mbpd on wee.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil exports from Baltic and Black Sea terminals fell 330,176 barrels per day (bpd) in the second week of March to 1.72 million bpd, Petro-Logistics said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Despite the fall, the total was still 411,116 bpd higher than the same week last year.</p>
<p>The Geneva-based consultancy, tracking tanker movements, said crude exports from Baltic and Black Sea ports fell 365,902 bpd on the week to 917,750 bpd, still 187,302 bpd above the same week last year.</p>
<p>Gas oil exports, however, rose 67,766 bpd to 474,451 bpd but still lagged year-ago levels by 4,101 bpd.</p>
<p>Heavy fuel exports fell 25,843 bpd to 279,315 bpd but were 198,062 bpd higher than in the same week last year.</p>
<p>The following table provided by Petro-Logistics lists a breakdown in metric tonnes of petroleum exports from the Baltic and Black Sea in the second week of March.</p>
